# --- F338 N2 note (appended 2026-08-21) ---
# This mutant is itself syntactically broken: removing the
# `_token = _os.environ.get("CAO_TERMINAL_TOKEN", "")` assignment while
# leaving the subsequent `if _token:` reference turns `_token` into an
# undefined name inside the `if "CAO_TERMINAL_ID" not in env:` branch.
# That branch is provably unreachable for command-bearing MCP configs
# (see wpcb-mutation-ledger/ledger.md, M16 section) -- bind_mcp_server_identity
# already sets CAO_TERMINAL_ID earlier in the same call, so the guard is
# always False and the broken reference never executes. The patch's own
# unreachable NameError is corroborating evidence -- independent of the
# dual-injection-path argument already in ledger.md -- for classifying M16
# as EQUIVALENT rather than survivable.
